1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Arvid Joungh''', not likely his real name, född i Skottland. Löjtnant vid amiralitetet '''1658'''. Borgare och handelsman i Borås 1659. Död 1708. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Says above''' he was Lt, in '''1658'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''It so happens''' that in 1658, [https://www.st-andrews.ac.uk/history/ssne/item.php?id=3810 in '''Alexander Young'''] was in Sweden: Alexander Young was a Scottish officer in Swedish service. He was a corporal in the noblemans' 
2 CONC corps in '''1658'''.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''So, i) we don't really''' believe to the Joungh hypothesis but consider Young to be more likely a name, then ii) from '''the leap from Alexander to Andrew is but butt'''. Next, iii) for now, we observe the year '''1658''' in bo
2 CONC th the links. Or in both the profiles! Given that both the profiles mention the very same year, there has to be a significance to that particular year. iv) '''Better yet. There's''' a resemblance with regard as to why that year co
2 CONC mes up. That's when he retired. It's more like "he was officer until 1658" than he was an officer in 1658. Chances for the year to be just random get slimmer...
2 CONT
2 CONT Gift med Anna Halfvardsdotter, född 1632, död 1720 Dalbogården och begraven 1720-07-10.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Cedersparre_nr_1511 '''Arvid Joungh'''], stamfar '''Cedersparre''' n:o 1511. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://runeberg.org/anrep/1/0434.html '''''Arvid'''''] född i Skottland. Löjtnant vid amiralitetet 1658. Borgare och handelsman i Borås 1659. Död 1708. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In''' [https://sabercathost.com/9oS9/Donner_-_Scottish_families_in_Finland_and_Sweden.pdf Scottish Families in Finland and Sweden], professor [https://www.geni.com/people/Otto-Donner/6000000000099938506 '''Otto Donner'''] write
2 CONC s (p. 43) Arvid's name as "'''Youngh'''." Could be "'''Young'''," too. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''As far as the''' first name in concerned, '''Arvid''' is not a Scottish name. It's a Nordic name. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''If I had to guess''', our '''Arvid Joung''' here is '''Andrew Young'''. Or something of the sort. 
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT <br/><br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
